<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Knives</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1799–1800</span> · Also known as War of Knives</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Knives was a civil war in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-domingue">Saint-Domingue</a> in 1799–1800 between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toussaint-louverture">Toussaint Louverture</a>, who controlled the north and west, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andre-rigaud">André Rigaud</a>, leader of the free people of colour in the south. Toussaint's forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jean-jacques-dessalines">Jean-Jacques Dessalines</a> overran the south, and Rigaud left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1800. The victory gave Toussaint control of the whole colony.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-knives.jpg" alt="War of the Knives" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown, Image publisher: Chez Jean rue Jean de Beauvais, No. 10, Paris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toussaint_L%27Ouverture.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
